# Exact/partial substrings that are allowed to match secret-like patterns.
# Prefer keeping this list small. Prefer fixing fixtures to look obviously fake.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored.

# DBHub driver/session tests assert how credentials are URL-encoded into a DSN,
# so they must contain a `user:password@` URL. The db-url-with-password rule
# matches any such URL regardless of how fake the values look, so these fixture
# values are allowlisted. Note the rule's match ends at the `@`, so an entry can
# never include the host — only the user:password portion.
bi%20reader:p%40ss%2Fword
bi%20reader:pw@
reader:pw@
